2. High-level implementation claim
----------------------------------

The current prototype should be described as:

  A scoped NVMe Simple Copy emulator and evaluation framework for NVMeVirt,
  not a complete NVMe 2.x implementation and not a production SSD firmware
  model.

Defensible research claim:

  Simple Copy is not just opcode plumbing. A faithful evaluation needs
  host-visible capability advertisement, command validation, host traffic
  avoidance, target-side media/FTL cost, benchmark byte accounting, and
  negative controls separating useful offload from merely moving work into the
  device.

Supported target classes:
  - CONFIG_NVMEVIRT_NVM:
      latency-only NVM target with host-visible backing-memory copy.
  - CONFIG_NVMEVIRT_SSD:
      conventional page-mapped SSD target with source-read timing, internal
      write-buffer timing without PCIe DMA, destination remap/program timing,
      and exact host-visible backing-memory copy.

Intentionally unsupported:
  - multi-namespace copy,
  - source namespace identifiers (snsids),
  - metadata/protection information,
  - nonzero directive fields,
  - Copy Descriptor Format other than 0h,
  - power-fail atomicity,
  - filesystem integration, including native F2FS/copy_file_range semantics,
  - production/commercial SSD firmware behavior.


