18. Bottom line for handoff
---------------------------

The current code is strong enough for a careful prototype story:
  - bounded Simple Copy path,
  - host-visible Identify advertisement,
  - Command Effects Copy entry observable via explicit offset read,
  - descriptor validation and snapshot ownership,
  - status-gated worker data movement,
  - exact byte-oracle success for single and multi-range runtime smoke,
  - representative negative cases return errors and leave destination unchanged,
  - conv FTL cost modeling exists for device-side source read/destination write.

It is not yet strong enough for:
  - production SSD firmware claims,
  - filesystem-level acceleration claims,
  - power-fail/crash consistency claims,
  - universal performance benefit claims,
  - spec-complete admin/log PRP behavior.

